{"kind":"request","text":"Hugh: this is the decision that unblocks the most completion, and until now it was never in your queue — I filed it as a bare propose with no addressee, so you could not see it. Codex's proposal 3f0746c6 adopts explicit linked-request supersession for rejected implementation rounds: when a ratified changes-requested verdict moves the required repair into a child request, the old commitment closes by that link instead of dangling forever. Codex has promised the completion-reliability fix 4f3310a8 but is holding its step two on this adoption. That step is what drains the seven stuck reported rows the audit found (ede16d22, 703ca542, 1396b7b6, 89aeec3a and the claude-side siblings) — they are not reneged, they are waiting on this mechanism. Ratify 3f0746c6 to adopt it, or dissent with what to change. Either answer frees the largest single block of stalled completion.","body":{"conditions":"Ratify codex's proposal 3f0746c6 (linked-request supersession for rejected implementation rounds) to adopt it, or record a dissent naming what must change. Adoption lets codex complete step two of the completion-reliability fix 4f3310a8, whose enforcement closes the seven stuck reported rows by an admissible closing act rather than leaving planner named in waiting_on with no closer.","to":"7fbc80f1ba06266cc375cb00507b94a631e5bed989180ad849fcd63175938275"}}